{"created": "2023-02-20T21:39:58.051466+00:00", "modified": "2023-02-22T02:26:48.006566+00:00", "id": 7657814, "conceptrecid": "7657813", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7657814", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.7657813", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7657814", "metadata": {"title": "10-Hz cross-spectral matrices from intracranial electrode recordings before and after loss of consciousness during propofol-induced general anesthesia", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7657814", "publication_date": "2023-02-20", "description": "<p>Companion resources associated with the publication, &quot;Propofol disrupts alpha dynamics in functionally distinct thalamocortical networks during loss of consciousness&quot; (in press) (DOI: 10.1073/pnas.2207831120)</p>\n\n<p>https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2022.04.05.487190v1.full.pdf</p>\n\n<p>Contents:</p>\n\n<p>1. 10-Hz cross-spectral matrices computed from pre- and post-loss of consciousness epochs (see manuscript for details)</p>\n\n<p>2. Channel labels of matrix rows and columns</p>\n\n<p>3. Channel coordinates and Freesurfer structural labels in MNI space.</p>\n\n<p>4. Structural segmentations of thalamic nuclei in MNI152 space. (Thanks to Fischl Lab, Martinos Center.)</p>\n\n<p>Patient demographics are listed in Supporting Information for the PNAS publication.</p>\n\n<p>For diffusion images used in the publication, please refer to the WU-Minn Human Connectome Project, using matches listed in the manuscript&#39;s Supporting Information.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Weiner, Veronica S", "affiliation": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Zhou, David W", "affiliation": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-9635-0472"}, {"name": "Kahali, Pegah", "affiliation": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Stephen, Emily P", "affiliation": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0003-1978-9622"}, {"name": "Peterfreund, Robert A", "affiliation": "Massach